      "writtenOn": "2024-10-16T17:33:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, after collecting boot logs and talking with willmcvicker@, the problem appears to be that pixel drivers directly rely on the state of the original phy structures in the dwc3 struct. With this patch, the usb2_generic_phy and usb3_generic_phy structs are not being initialized.\n\nWithout looking in deeper, I have concerns that just initializing these would not be enough, it would be required to keep them in sync.",
      "parentUuid": "2aa28d14_45059b6a",
      "revId": "df8979c9403a97750c577ba00f50535817583c6e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "84a72b65_f411cd54",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1957137
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-22T08:05:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Without looking in deeper, I have concerns that just initializing these would not be enough, it would be required to keep them in sync.\n\nMeaning ? IIUC, we are not using the variables at all.\n\nWe are using \"dwc-\u003eusbX_generic_phy[0]\" instead of them which are initialized properly.",
      "parentUuid": "27c4627d_9b17e245",
      "revId": "df8979c9403a97750c577ba00f50535817583c6e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e1772bb_7811a2d3",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1981633
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-22T15:37:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because `struct dwc3` is part of the KMI, the meaning and use of the existing fields must be maintained, as, while this driver may no longer be using \"dwc-\u003eusbX_generic_phy[0]\", other vendors have drivers which rely on this field behaving the way it always has.\n\nYour current change is still breaking this KMI contract as this field is essentially abandoned in the dwc3 struct and moved to the vendor struct.",
      "parentUuid": "84a72b65_f411cd54",
      "revId": "df8979c9403a97750c577ba00f50535817583c6e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a753f6b3_5117b17d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1957137
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-23T02:24:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The change replaces usage of \"dwc-\u003eusbX_generic_phy\" with \"vdwc-\u003eusbX_generic_phy[0]\" at all places and this takes effect for everyone using the driver.\n\nVendors only need this structure to hold reference to the phy, it doesn\u0027t matter AFAIK if it gets stored in \"dwc-\u003e_phy\" variable or  \"vdwc-\u003e_phy[0]\" variable right ? \n\n\n`other vendors have drivers which rely on this field behaving the way it always has`\n\nDo you mean wrapper driver in their downstream kernels or changes in their downstream kernels are dependent on dwc-\u003eusbX_generic_phy and hence its usage needs to kept same ?",
      "parentUuid": "9e1772bb_7811a2d3",
      "revId": "df8979c9403a97750c577ba00f50535817583c6e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
